WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:15,640
Oh, to add to the glucose question a month ago or so, I'd go to my colleges for my injections

00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:20,600
and before getting them, they'd take my blood around 2 p.m. by glucose, who'd come out

00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,840
at about 82 hours after eating lunch.

00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:30,280
Okay, so little known fact is that your glucose, if you took your glucose right after you ate

00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:35,120
lunch, even if it wasn't a high carb lunch, your glucose will spike.

00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:42,120
It's normal, that's a post-gradual glucose test, and it's normal to spike up, but then it

00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:45,840
drops down, and then it balances out.

00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:50,320
So that's why you wanted, if you're going to be taking your glucose levels to measure

00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:55,520
your glucose levels, you want to take it at a 10 or 12 hour fast on a regular basis, don't

00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:01,360
do this because it'll give you a false rating of, oh, it's down to 80, that's almost in

00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:07,960
the 70s, that's really good, yeah, because it's just dropped, it plummeted from a high

00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:15,040
after eating, and now it'll go up 80, 90, 95, and then that will be your normal.

00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:23,280
So it's not a fair assessment of really where your glucose levels are on average.

